23. Dollar Thinking vs Pip Thinking
Dollar Thinking — Wrong
"मुझे आज $50 चाहिए"
→ Greed-based trading
→ Random lot size
→ No proper risk management
→ Account blow की तरफ
Pip Thinking — Right
"मुझे आज 50 pips का clean setup चाहिए"
→ Process-based trading
→ Proper lot size calculation
→ Risk defined in pips
→ Consistent results
Example
Two traders, same setup:
Gold move = $3 = 300 pips

Trader A (Dollar thinking):
0.10 lot लिया क्योंकि "$30 profit nice है"
Profit = $30

Trader B (Pip thinking):
Account = $1000
Risk 1% = $10
SL = 100 pips
Lot = 0.10
Profit (300 pips) = $30

Same result, लेकिन Trader B का approach controlled है
Next trade में Trader B same discipline follow करेगा
Trader A नहीं करेगा
